         .page-expand-close buttons to the body.kmb-page-expanded class
         (site.css does the filling/hiding). Self-guards on pages without
         either button, so loading it globally is safe. -->
    <script type="module" src="~/js/lib/expand-page.js"></script>
    <!-- M35 (ADR 0164) — the kiosk-mode auto-cycle / auto-refresh state
         machine (client/lib/kiosk.ts, tsc-built). Drives the /kiosk display's
         #kiosk-stage iframe: advances the visible slide to the next (wrapping
         to the first) every data-view-interval, and re-points the iframe src
         (re-running the surface's own Read decision on the frozen seam) every
         data-refresh-interval; a slide the viewer cannot see shows the
         localized kiosk.slide_denied shape (no leak, no 404). Self-guards on
         pages without #kiosk-stage, so loading it globally is safe (the
         expand-page.js idiom). No new npm package / build step (M35·7). -->
    <script type="module" src="~/js/lib/kiosk.js"></script>
    <!-- M37 (ADR 0167) — the personal-note modal (client/lib/note-modal.ts,
         tsc-built). Wires the _NoteButton partial's Bootstrap modal to the
         JSON API endpoints (GET/POST/PUT/DELETE /notes/api/...): add /
         edit / delete a note without leaving the page. Self-guards on pages
         without the [data-note-button] anchor (every page except the ten
         detail surfaces), so loading it globally is safe (the expand-page.js
         idiom). -->
    <script type="module" src="~/js/lib/note-modal.js"></script>
    <!-- M10 U03 (ADR 0107 D5/D10) — the PWA install affordance + the
         service-worker registration (client/lib/pwa-install.ts, tsc-built).
         Registers /sw.js (U02's passive SW) and reveals the #pwa-install
         label source as one quiet fixed button on beforeinstallprompt;
         a clean no-op where the browser never fires it (iOS). -->
    <script type="module" src="~/js/lib/pwa-install.js"></script>
    <!-- Nav-row overflow fold (client/lib/nav-more-fold.ts, tsc-built — ADR 0113):
         in the variant-B "top row" nav, folds Community + Groups into the More
         menu when the row doesn't fit, and back when there is room. Self-guards
         (no-op) in variant C, signed-out, and where the data-nav-* hooks are
         absent, so loading it globally is safe. -->
    <script type="module" src="~/js/lib/nav-more-fold.js"></script>
    <!-- Rail label expander (client/lib/rail-expander.ts, tsc-built — variant C):
         toggles the body's .kmb-rail-expanded class when the .kmb-rail-expander
         button is clicked (site.css widens the rail + reveals each section's
         .kmb-rail-label + updates the content shift). The preference persists
         in localStorage. Self-guards (no-op) in variant B and where the
         expander button is absent, so loading it globally is safe. -->
    <script type="module" src="~/js/lib/rail-expander.js"></script>
    @* P0-6 (translation audit) — the client-JS strings bundle: the closed
